    "turn_text": "I appreciate it, man. And you know, it's it's sad guys, because I've had I've had that question asked of me, what's it going to take? what's it going to take Eli for you to for you to come on board for you to get on board the team and do what we need to get done here. And so, you know, I mean, it's, it's just, it's, it's sad, you know, and I'm just, you know, going to tell your audience like I don't consider myself a good congressman at all. I would have never saw myself running for this spot. Matter of fact, I would you know, as a dad and somebody raising kids in this country, somebody who's fought for this country, I would want our congressmen and women and our representatives, our senators to be way more qualified than I am. But when I looked around at the landscape and I looked at the people that, you know, are running and when I listen to what they say and then I see them go up to Washington DC and do something completely different. I'm like, Well, Eli, you may not, you know, you may not think you're qualified, but at least you won't become that. And that's a start right there. And so, you know, it is what, like I said, I feel blessed in a way in, you know, a lot of warriors. can understand what I'm saying. There's a part of me that feels alive again, like I'm back in the fight in a completely different unit, fighting a completely different mission. But then again, I'm not going to lie and tell you guys that the outlook is good because it's not.",
