    "turn_text": "so easy for your congressman or your senator to come back to the district or the state and be like, oh, I'm doing all these wonderful things. And you just believe them because they're great at talking. But because you haven't looked at their voting record, you haven't. And that's an entire onion all by itself. Oftentimes, people will just look at what the name of the bill says, and it'll be the Bipartisan Border Security Act. And you'll be like, oh, that sounds great. But you won't really go look into it. And therefore, you're even more easy to manipulate. And they name stuff all the time up there, and they name bills all the time up there that do the exact opposite of what they say. And so it actually takes an engaged, educated populace and citizenry to like Make this country actually go who will sin representatives to Washington DC that will actually represent them But right now we don't have that and matter of fact in many ways I think we're going the opposite direction because a lot of kids aren't even being taught American history or civics anymore And I think it's on purpose I think they want they want to dumb us down like you you hear all the time people in pundits and you know Americans talking about, oh, we have a democracy. Well, do we? Or do we have a constitutional republic, right? And there's a big difference. And so it is important that people actually tune in and are educated and paying attention or we're going to keep sending the same idiots up to Washington, D.C., who talk a good game and then just become part of the uni party or the swamp and do the exact opposite that they tell you they're doing when they're back home.",
