    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "No, you're right, man. And you did ask me, hey, what's one of the surprising things that you've seen? And, you know, I do want to inject some levity and some humanity into this conversation, man, because, you know, there's, there's some Democrats out there that, you know, it's like, I'm obviously a Republican, but there's some Democrats out there that like I love them as human beings and people and I'll have conversations with them just like you would with your your ant ethel you know and so I'm not trying to you know I'm not trying to villainize anybody but that was surprising to me because when you go into such a hyper-partisan polarized environment you think that you're never going to be able to find common ground with anybody you're never even going to be able to have a conversation with anybody on the opposite team or the other side. And I have found that not to be true. There is something to be said for, you know, when we're not fighting with each other over policies or in committee hearings, you know, a lot of these people are, they're just regular people. Yeah, I may not agree with, you know, with them and their worldview or their policies, but that is interesting to find common ground with them and be like, wow, I thought that person or he or she would be way different than my perception of them was.",
