    "turn_text": "Yeah, no, I mean, you're 100% right and it's everywhere I look, whether I look at Secretary of Mayorkas, who's running, you know, Department of Homeland Security. You know, I'm actually surprised that we were able to get rid of Director Cheadle from the Secret Service. Um, you know, but it does seem, and I heard Eric Prince talking about this on Sean Ryan's show a couple of weeks ago. He was talking about we have this culture where nobody's ever held accountable anymore and where people consistently fail upwards. And I, you guys are. Ryan, you're right. I think you nailed it. It's one of the biggest reasons that I think back in the day when people were held accountable and actually fired when they did a horrible, crummy job. People were cautious and hesitant about doing a horrible job, but now they're like, it doesn't matter. As long as I know the right people and I'm in with the, you know, the elite or the power brokers in this country and I, you know, I do what I'm told and I follow orders and I don't cross them. They'll continue to promote me. And I think again, going back to the American people being checked out and complacent, I think that's one of the reasons they're able to do it. Because I mean, it's just like Kamala Harris right now, right? Like a couple of years ago, Kamala Harris was the most unpopular vice president in the history, not even a couple of years ago.",
