    "turn_text": "Now the machine has gotten completely behind her and she's like, you know, this rock star, right? And people are, you know, getting energized. And I think part of it is because they went from somebody that was. so horrible, you know, in Joe Biden and that, you know, just set aside policy for a second and look at the guy could barely walk on stage. He could barely put together since he didn't know where he was half the time. I mean, if the entire world, not just the country saw that debate and people had known what his mental state was for a very long time. And so they went from this guy that, you know, would have been, I think probably wouldn't have been able to drive a car in many states being their commander in chief, their nominee to at least somebody who can not trip and fall off the stage. And so it's just wild, man. But when I look at Kamala Harris, there's no way she would have ever gotten the nomination had she had to go through the process and get win a primary and you know get votes from the american people how do i know that because she tried to do it and she you know she's unpocked she's wildly unpopular",
