    "turn_idx": 131,
    "turn_text": "How they jumped all over us and ripped our faces off on national television. And I was like, okay, you know, it's good because then you figure out, you start figuring out who's who in the zoo, who's legitimate. who's a fraud and the list of who's legitimate gets smaller and smaller by the day. And you find out, I found out sadly guys, and I will mention specifics here, but some people that I had respected, I'd even done their programs in the past, ripped our faces off and destroyed us because they were getting paid to do it. They were getting paid. And so it goes back to the same, you know, the same thing. But like I said, if you believe, if you go into this, I think knowing that you don't have a long shelf life and eventually you're going to get taken out, I think it makes you, it just gives you the freedom to, you know, do whatever you can. And you know, the sad thing, Clark, I mean, you and I, I've known you for a couple years now and, Like I used to maybe naively think that my integrity was one thing that nobody could take from me. And as I've gotten into politics and as Ryan's talking about AI, I no longer believe that anymore because I've seen how powerful the machine is. I've seen how people manipulate, you know, whether it's a video clip or a voiceover or something like that. And so You know, it is scary and, you know, I may not make it. I may not make it out of this, you know, with everything intact that I wanted to, but I don't know, man. I'm hoping that I'm, you know, I do believe it's worth it. I do believe it's worth fighting for. Do you want to see my kids and, you know, other, other youngsters all around the country? you know, of all colors of all walks of life. I hate that I even have to say that anymore, but just Americans grow up with what we grew up with. And, you know, I feel like if they don't get to, it's because we didn't do enough. And so if that means that you have to throw something down, like your integrity or your reputation and put it on the line, then I just, you know, and this goes back to my faith, you know, because, you know, I'm not big on following this world. I'm being on following my Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ who was, you know, murdered, lied about and, you know, crucified, beaten. And, and so, and I'm nothing like it. I accepted him into my life because I am a sinner and I couldn't do that for myself. And so I needed a savior and I'll just put that out on your show. But, but hey, man, if I don't make it out of this with my integrity intact, I suppose there are worst, worst fates out there, you know,",
